.TH JSONCHECK 1 "November 2026" "jsoncheck" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
jsoncheck \- JSON syntax validator and formatter

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jsoncheck validate
.I file

.B jsoncheck format
.RB [ \-\-pretty | \-\-compact ]
.I file

.B jsoncheck \-\-help

.B jsoncheck \-\-version

.SH DESCRIPTION
jsoncheck is a command-line utility for validating and
formatting JSON documents using the cJSON library.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B validate
Check the syntax of a JSON file. If the document is invalid,
report the line, column and byte offset of the error.

.TP
.B format
Validate and print a formatted JSON document to standard output.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-pretty
Print JSON with indentation and line breaks.

.TP
.B \-\-compact
Print JSON without unnecessary whitespace.

.TP
.B \-\-help
Display help information.

.TP
.B \-\-version
Display the program version.

.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is located at:

.I /etc/jsoncheck/jsoncheck.conf

Supported values:

.B format=pretty

.B format=compact

The default mode is pretty. Missing configuration files are
ignored. Command-line format options take precedence over
configuration settings.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution.

.TP
.B 1
Invalid JSON, file error or configuration error.

.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line arguments.

.SH EXAMPLES
Validate a JSON file:

.B jsoncheck validate example.json

Print formatted JSON:

.B jsoncheck format example.json

Print compact JSON:

.B jsoncheck format \-\-compact example.json

